  "body": "Gecko uses `area { display: none !important }`.\n\nBlink used to create a box for `<area>`, but no longer does as of https://issues.chromium.org/issues/41140071\n\nReason is that it is confusing if an `<area>` has a layout box, because it may have two roles in the accessibility tree (what does it mean if it has nested content etc).\n\nLacking any use case for actually displaying an `<area>` element, maybe we should consider just spec'ing the Gecko behavior, if other browsers are willing to follow?\n\nSee also https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=725921.\n\ncc: @rjesup @hjanuschka @mstensho @zcorpan @annevk @jcsteh ",
